id: pm-euqm7x
title: Windows published-release verifier test can preempt its own readiness and cleanup contract
description: "Merged-main CI run 33867283305 intermittently killed the published HTTP evaluator after 10 seconds while the evaluator contract permits 15 seconds of readiness plus 2 seconds of cleanup. spawnSync then returned a nonzero/null result with empty stderr, hiding whether discovery or cleanup failed. The exact failed job reran green, proving nondeterminism on byte-identical source rather than resolving the invalid timeout ordering."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-04T11:51:40.569Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T12:08:08.320Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T12:02:13.639Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T12:02:13.639Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "The test-specific evaluator readiness bound is lower than the outer process timeout by at least the full shutdown grace; timeout arithmetic is asserted explicitly; the expected invalid-discovery path and port-reuse cleanup remain required; focused, full coverage, static, and hosted Windows gates pass."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make the Windows published-artifact regression fail only on verifier behavior and always preserve a diagnostic before the harness deadline
value: Merged-main release readiness becomes deterministic and actionable instead of depending on hosted runner timing
impact: Prevents false red release blockers and silent empty-stderr terminations in the Windows oracle
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: "GitHub Actions windows-latest, Node 24"
resolution: "The surviving-server regression now supplies a 4-second evaluator readiness bound under a 10-second harness deadline, derives the real 2-second shutdown grace from the generated evaluator, asserts sufficient headroom, and fails explicitly if spawnSync terminates the evaluator."
expected_result: The evaluator always reaches its invalid-discovery diagnostic and governed process-tree cleanup before the test harness deadline on Windows.
actual_result: Focused verifier tests and exact repo coverage pass; the former 10s < 15s + 2s ordering is replaced by 10s >= 4s + 2s with 4 seconds of remaining headroom.
regression: true
